---
layout: default
---
<div class="post">
  <header class="post-header about-hero">
    {% if page.profile and page.profile.image %}
      <div class="about-hero-photo">
        {% assign profile_image_path = page.profile.image | prepend: 'assets/img/' %}
        {% if page.profile.image_circular %}
          {% assign profile_image_class = 'img-fluid z-depth-1 rounded-circle' %}
        {% else %}
          {% assign profile_image_class = 'img-fluid z-depth-1 rounded' %}
        {% endif %}
        {%
          include figure.liquid loading="eager" path=profile_image_path class=profile_image_class sizes="200px" alt="Arash Jalil Khabbazi"
          cache_bust=true
        %}
      </div>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="about-hero-name">
      <h1 class="post-title">
        {% if site.title == 'blank' %}
          <span class="font-weight-bold">{{ site.first_name }}</span> {{ site.middle_name }}
          {{ site.last_name }}
        {% else %}
          {{ site.title }}
        {% endif %}
      </h1>
      <p class="desc">{{ page.subtitle }}</p>
      <div class="about-contact">
        <a href="mailto:{{ site.data.socials.email | encode_email }}"><i class="fa-solid fa-envelope" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>{{ site.data.socials.email }}</span></a>
        <a href="tel:+17657672058"><i class="fa-solid fa-phone" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>+1 (765) 767-2058</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% if page.availability %}
      <div class="availability">
        <div class="availability-text">{{ page.availability | markdownify }}</div>
        <div class="availability-actions">
          <a class="availability-btn availability-btn--primary" href="{{ '/assets/pdf/resume-ajk.pdf' | relative_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><i class="fa-solid fa-file-lines" aria-hidden="true"></i>resume</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  </header>

  <article>
    <div class="clearfix">{{ content }}</div>

    <!-- Research: one number and a lead line, then the three PhD phases on a rail,
         each card linking to its phase on the research page -->
    <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <a href="{{ '/research/' | relative_url }}" class="heading-link">Research</a>
    </h2>
    <div class="home-research-intro">
      <div class="home-stat">
        <span class="home-stat-label"><strong>Buildings</strong> use</span>
        <a class="home-stat-num" href="https://www.iea.org/news/making-buildings-more-efficient-offers-a-major-opportunity-to-bring-down-energy-bills-and-reduce-emissions">~30%</a>
        <span class="home-stat-label">of the world&rsquo;s energy</span>
      </div>
      <div class="home-research-text">
        <p class="home-research-lead">Much of that depends on how their systems are controlled. <strong>Advanced control</strong>, such as <strong>predictive control</strong> and <strong>reinforcement learning</strong>, can save energy and money, but it rarely reaches real buildings at scale.</p>
        <p class="home-research-statement">My PhD research aims to advance the state of the art of practical automation systems for efficient, occupant- and grid-interactive buildings. I&rsquo;m developing and demonstrating scalable algorithms in real buildings, minimizing data and engineering requirements. At Purdue, I also work with the Energy and Utilities team on reducing peak cooling demand in campus buildings.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="home-phases">
      <a class="home-phase home-phase--done" href="{{ '/research/' | relative_url }}#phase-1">
        <span class="home-phase-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
        <span class="home-phase-card">
          <span class="home-phase-media"><img class="home-phase-img" src="{{ '/assets/img/research/field-demos-fig1.webp' | relative_url }}" alt="" loading="lazy"></span>
          <span class="home-phase-body">
            <span class="home-phase-title">Field evidence<i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right home-phase-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
            <span class="home-phase-text">About 4% of advanced control papers test in a real building. 71% of the tests use potentially unreliable protocols. The other 29% report 15&ndash;22% energy savings.</span>
            <span class="home-phase-status"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check" aria-hidden="true"></i>Completed</span>
          </span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="home-phase" href="{{ '/research/' | relative_url }}#phase-2">
        <span class="home-phase-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
        <span class="home-phase-card">
          <span class="home-phase-media"><img class="home-phase-img" src="{{ '/assets/img/research/savings-thumb.webp' | relative_url }}" alt="" loading="lazy"></span>
          <span class="home-phase-body">
            <span class="home-phase-title">Savings measurement<i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right home-phase-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
            <span class="home-phase-text">Tests that control only part of a building overstate energy savings, sometimes several times over, because heat transfer from neighboring zones goes uncounted.</span>
            <span class="home-phase-status"><span class="home-phase-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>In progress</span>
          </span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="home-phase" href="{{ '/research/' | relative_url }}#phase-3">
        <span class="home-phase-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
        <span class="home-phase-card">
          <span class="home-phase-media"><img class="home-phase-img" src="{{ '/assets/img/research/campus-thumb.webp' | relative_url }}" alt="" loading="lazy"></span>
          <span class="home-phase-body">
            <span class="home-phase-title">Control algorithms<i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right home-phase-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
            <span class="home-phase-text">Developing learning-based control that needs little data and engineering effort, and testing it on reducing the peak cooling demand of the Purdue campus.</span>
            <span class="home-phase-status"><span class="home-phase-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>In progress</span>
          </span>
        </span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <!-- Cards fade in one after another when the row scrolls into view. The hiding class is
         added here, so without scripts (or with reduced motion) the cards simply show. -->
    <script>
      (function () {
        var row = document.querySelector(".home-phases");
        if (!row || !("IntersectionObserver" in window)) return;
        if (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches) return;
        row.classList.add("home-phases--reveal");
        var observer = new IntersectionObserver(
          function (entries) {
            for (var i = 0; i < entries.length; i++) {
              if (entries[i].isIntersecting) {
                row.classList.add("is-visible");
                observer.disconnect();
                return;
              }
            }
          },
          { threshold: 0.15 }
        );
        observer.observe(row);
      })();
    </script>

    <!-- News -->
    {% if page.announcements and page.announcements.enabled %}
      <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <a href="{{ '/news/' | relative_url }}" class="heading-link">News</a>
      </h2>

      <div class="home-panel">{% include news.liquid limit=true %}</div>
    {% endif %}

    <!-- Latest posts -->
    {% if page.latest_posts and page.latest_posts.enabled %}
      <h2>
        <a href="{{ '/blog/' | relative_url }}" class="heading-link">latest posts</a>
      </h2>
      {% include latest_posts.liquid %}
    {% endif %}

    <!-- Selected papers -->
    {% if page.selected_papers %}
      <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <a href="{{ '/publications/' | relative_url }}" class="heading-link">Select Publications</a>
      </h2>
      <div class="home-panel">{% include selected_papers.liquid %}</div>
    {% endif %}

    <!-- Social -->
    {% if page.social %}
      <div class="social">
        <div class="contact-icons">{% include social.liquid %}</div>

        <div class="contact-note">{{ site.contact_note }}</div>
      </div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if site.newsletter and site.newsletter.enabled and site.footer_fixed %}
      {% include newsletter.liquid center=true %}
    {% endif %}
  </article>
</div>
